GLM-5.3-Flash (glm5next) CPU library, step 4 of 5: cell-split MQA flash attention for short query batches.
NOT deployed. CHANGES NUMERICAL OUTPUT (toward the float64 result). GGML_F18_FEATURES bit 0, default off.
Apply after glm5next-pool-result-cache.patch (or after glm5next-kpool-wide.patch; the hunks do not overlap).

What the stock kernel does. With an F16 KV cache, ggml_compute_forward_flash_attn_ext_f16_one_chunk accumulates V in an FP16
buffer (VKQ16, ggml_vec_mad_f16). Over ~2,000 cells each addend is near or below the accumulator's rounding step, so the small
terms are dropped. It also walks the whole cache once per query-head row, converts Q to F16 for the dot product, and converts
each K/V row again for every head and query. This code is identical in upstream llama.cpp (checked at b23efaa2).

What this kernel does (absorbed MLA is MQA: one 512-wide K/V head, V aliases K, one f16 mask row per query):
  every worker finds the cells ANY query can see (AVX-512BW scan of the mask), takes a contiguous slice of them, converts that
  slice of K to F32 once, and computes partial softmax sums for all query-head rows with two GEMMs per 64-cell tile
  (scores = Q x K^T, then V accumulation), all in F32. One barrier, then the per-worker partials are merged per row.
  The K tile is transposed with a 16x16 AVX-512 network; a scalar transpose cost HALF the kernel before that.

Accuracy, relative RMS error against a float64 reference computed from the same tensors:
  synthetic, 2,051 of 4,096 cells visible, 3 queries x 16 heads:   stock 6.4e-3    this kernel 2.4e-7
  pure upstream build (b23efaa2), same program:                     stock 6.4e-3
  IN SITU, 8-layer proxy of the real model, real cache and masks (-DF18_FA_VERIFY recomputes each node both ways):
      1 query     stock 9.6e-4 mean           this kernel 7.3e-7 mean
      3 queries   stock 1.26e-2 mean, 2.5e-2 max   this kernel 6.4e-7 mean, 1.4e-6 max   (the speculative verify batch)
Speed of the op, 15 workers, one socket: verify shape 1.16 -> 0.23 ms; dense draft shape 0.49 -> 0.17 ms; 32,768-cell cache with
2,051 visible 1.65 -> 0.24 ms (the context term of the op is gone). In the server the op measures ~0.47 ms per DSA layer
(cold scratch between calls) against ~1.1 ms including its barrier before.

Full model, window w1 2026-09-20, same loaded process, actual Codex requests through the Paseo wrapper, greedy, 3,998-token input,
four runs per mode, this patch together with topk-select-tie-fallback.patch:
      production-equivalent  16.22 / 16.26 / 16.27 / 16.20   mean 16.236 tok/s   157 of 196 drafts accepted
      both kernels on        17.05 / 17.24 / 17.30 / 17.30   mean 17.225 tok/s   158 of 196                  (+6.1%)
Because the stock kernel is ~1% off, generated text differs from production: 2 of 10 short factual prompts gave the same 24-token
string, and token log-probabilities moved by up to 0.46 on a 7K-token prompt. Byte parity with production is therefore NOT the
gate for this patch; the float64 comparison is. The window library was built before the ifdef'd verify block was added
(same code otherwise). Queries above 16 tokens (prefill) keep the stock tiled path.

